Project Identity & Architectural Development Attribution:
HINATA (ひなた) is an independent local autonomous AI desktop companion platform designed, architected, and developed by Mohammad Huzaifa. The project integrates a local multimodal AI brain, semantic memory, knowledge-graph reasoning, agentic tools, voice synthesis, proactive behavior, and an embodied VRM desktop companion into a unified on-device system.

The repository may incorporate, vendor, or reference third-party open-source software, model weights, model variants, runtime components, and other external materials. Those components remain subject to their respective upstream licenses and terms. This license governs the HINATA project source code, original architecture, original documentation, original UI/UX, branding, and other original materials owned by Mohammad Huzaifa, except where expressly stated otherwise.

