1. **No Execution or Deployment**: You may not compile, build, run, host, deploy, or execute HINATA or any protected HINATA component on public or private servers, local devices, virtual machines, containers, cloud infrastructure, mobile devices, emulators, or production systems.
2. **No Code Copying or Plagiarism**: You may not copy, duplicate, replicate, republish, paste, hotlink, or otherwise reproduce any protected portion of the HINATA codebase, algorithms, architecture, API design, schemas, prompts, agent protocols, or implementation details.
3. **No Derivative Works or Forks**: You may not create, compile, distribute, publish, or sublicense derivative works, modified builds, forks, plugins, extensions, ports, or complementary implementations derived from protected HINATA materials.
4. **No Component Extraction or Integration**: You may not extract, reuse, or integrate protected HINATA components—including the agentic orchestration logic, memory/RAG architecture, knowledge-graph implementation, tool framework, sandboxing logic, mood/proactivity systems, desktop companion implementation, UI system, or other original subsystems—into third-party software or services.
5. **No Commercial Exploitation**: You may not sell, lease, rent, license, sublicense, commercialize, monetize, or otherwise use protected HINATA materials to generate direct or indirect revenue.
6. **No Asset, UI, or Branding Theft**: You may not reuse HINATA logos, names, visual assets, avatar presentation, UI components, design systems, animations, color systems, typography treatments, branding, screenshots, or other protected presentation materials.
7. **No Reverse Engineering or Security Attacks**: You may not reverse-engineer, decompile, disassemble, extract protected implementation details, or conduct penetration testing, vulnerability scanning, fuzzing, denial-of-service testing, or other attacks against HINATA infrastructure or services.
8. **No AI / LLM Model Training**: Protected HINATA source code, architecture, documentation, prompts, comments, datasets, schemas, or original implementation materials may not be used as training inputs, fine-tuning corpora, evaluation corpora, or scraped datasets for LLMs, code-generation models, developer assistants, or other generative AI systems without written consent.
9. **No Unauthorized Academic Submission**: HINATA or any substantial portion of its protected materials may not be submitted as original work for academic credit, thesis evaluation, hackathons, grading, certification, or similar educational purposes without prior written authorization from Mohammad Huzaifa.

